{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage","id":1538237,"title":"Quintessence and Tass Usage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-08T09:33:36-07:00","id":1538237,"title":"Quintessence and Tass Usage","content":"As usual, I am sorry if this is a conversation that has been done to death, but I want to double-check what I've managed to figure out over the last few days. And maybe the next person trying to find these answers via web-search will have a bit easier time!<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to get to run a game of M20 soon, so I'm trying to get a more comprehensive handle on the mechanics. One of the things that's been a bit confusing has been discussions around accessing Quintessence with the Prime Sphere. Between M20 Core and HDYDT(yes, I know, but I work with what I've got), it feels like there are some ambiguities about what you can do with each given level of Prime when it comes to using Quintessence and Tass.<br /> <br /> I think one of my main points of confusion comes from conflicting statements that I've found in M20 and HDYDT regarding Tass (and also Periapts):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Core, p.520</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A beginning study of Prime allows the mage to perceive and channel Quintessence from Nodes, Tass, Wonders, and magickal Effects. She may spot energetic ebbs and flows, can sense and at least try to read Resonance and Synergy signatures, and could also absorb Quintessence into her personal Pattern. Mages without at least one dot in Prime cannot absorb Quintessence beyond their Avatar Background rating. A Prime-skilled mage, however, may do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it sounds like you need at least Prime 1 in order to make use of Tass. It also doesn't help that they seem to be using the words &quot;absorb&quot; and &quot;channel&quot; in a casual sense here, while also using them in a slightly more official/technical capacity when referring to specific Effects using Prime 3, on M20 Core p.510. <br /> <br /> But then, in HDYDT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HDYDT, p.45</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Under normal circumstances, a mage with Tass, a Periapt, or a Matrix on his person can access that battery\u2019s Quintessence reflexively \u2013 that is, without using an additional Effect.</b> If that battery is within reach but not touching the character, he can use a Prime 2 Effect to get the energy. And if the battery is some distance away, he can use Correspondence 2/ Prime 2 in order to draw upon the energy within the Periapt.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Now it sounds like any Mage is capable of using Tass that they have on their person, without any ranks in the Prime Sphere (it also seems to imply that the &quot;Employ Periapt&quot; Effect listed on p.510 of M20 Core specifically refers to using over distance). <br /> <br /> So, the questions are as follows:<br /> <br /> 1) Can any Mage, without the Prime Sphere, consume edible Tass in order to add its Quintessence to their own Pattern? I feel like this is an idea I've encountered before, but I haven't found any specific rules or clarifications in M20, so far (the only specific memory I have is drinking Vitae for Quint from Blood Treachery, but I can't recall if that was supposed to be exceptional).<br /> <br /> 2) Do you need at least Prime 1 in order to use (inedible) Tass at all, or can any Mage use the Quintessence inside of Tass as long as they have it on their person?<br /> <br /> 3) What rank of Prime do you need to absorb the Quintessence out of (inedible) Tass and directly into your Pattern? Does that require Prime 3, or is Prime 1 enough as long as you are holding the Tass and remain within the Quintessence/turn limits imposed by the Avatar background? It kind of sounds like the Prime 3 reference on M20 Core p.520 is talking about absorbing at a distance, like the quote about Periapts from HDYDT mentioned above, but I'd appreciate a second opinion.<br /> <br /> Part of why I'm so focused on Tass is because I encountered some threads pointing out how working for Tass is one way that Cabals of Mages without access to a Node or high level Prime magic can still get the Quintessence they need for their spellcasting. The details of how said Mages can use the Tass they worked for are kind of important in that context.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for a mixture of M20 interpretations from more experienced players, but I'd also appreciate if people could point out older sources that provide better explanations. After getting some feedback, I'll probably try and write out a list of how you can use Quint and Tass with each rank of the Prime Sphere, hopefully something folks can easily refer to in the future if I don't make a mess of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T09:58:11-07:00","id":1538239,"title":"","content":"1. No. The most consistent thing is that you need Prime 3 to consume any quintessence. I personally dont agree with that and allow to use tass with Prime 1<br /> 2. As explained above.<br /> 3. Its Prime 3 as explained above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T12:29:07-07:00","id":1538247,"title":"","content":"Well, I think the rule for Nodes is that a mage can meditate in the presence of one to absorb Quint even without Prime, but the limit is the Avatar rating. With Prime 1 there isn't a limit anymore. Converting Tass, though, still takes Prime 3. While the description of Prime 1 does indicate otherwise, the first rank of Spheres generally doesn't augment a mage's capabilities like that. General Tass conversion should remain Rank 3.<br /> <br /> That said, using Prime 1 to absorb Tass by eating it (or in some other appropriate way consuming it) makes a lot of sense thematically. I think it might even be a rule in previous editions or in Awakening. If you want to rule that Prime 1 allows a mage to absorb the Quintessence of Tass when it is used/consumed in a dramatically appropriate mundane way, that would be quite reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T13:56:37-07:00","id":1538253,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Tass, how you use it is important.<br /> <br /> My understanding (I don't remember if and where I read it) is that Tass can be directly used in spellcasting, as long as it is done in an appropriate way. And that would make its Resonance very important to consider.<br /> <br /> So, let's say you have a vial of Vampire Blood counting as Tass, and you want to make mind-altering spell. One way to do so could be to inscribe runes in the tied up target's head with red ink, and then you incorporate the Vitae by using it as said ink. The resonance of the Vitae would be relevant in the casting, though, helping or hindering depending on what kinds of thoughts you want to create.<br /> <br /> This would be a Prime-Free use of Tass. Vampire Blood is a special case in that a Mage that consumes it will keep it as Vitae, which is Quintessence in itself, but most other Tass can't be consumed for later use without Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T15:06:17-07:00","id":1538258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538247#post1538247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think the rule for Nodes is that a mage can meditate in the presence of one to absorb Quint even without Prime, but the limit is the Avatar rating. With Prime 1 there isn't a limit anymore. Converting Tass, though, still takes Prime 3. While the description of Prime 1 does indicate otherwise, the first rank of Spheres generally doesn't augment a mage's capabilities like that. General Tass conversion should remain Rank 3.<br /> <br /> That said, using Prime 1 to absorb Tass by eating it (or in some other appropriate way consuming it) makes a lot of sense thematically. I think it might even be a rule in previous editions or in Awakening. If you want to rule that Prime 1 allows a mage to absorb the Quintessence of Tass when it is used/consumed in a dramatically appropriate mundane way, that would be quite reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the rules for meditating at Nodes and their relationship to Prime, they're pretty clear.<br /> <br /> There are a bunch of other weird things that you can do with Prime 1 that wouldn't normally be possible with the sensory nature of the first rank in a Sphere (I think I saw Ambrosia harrumphing about it in one thread I was reading? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). I've also wondered the same thing about getting Mind Shields with Mind 1. So I considered it an open question. But yeah, M20 can be a bit of a mess sometimes even in the basic description of the Spheres (e.g. arguments about that paragraph saying you need Matter or Life for teleporting small objects with Correspondence 2).<br /> <br /> I do think that my memories about being able to consume certain forms of Tass may be coming from my time with Awakening, entirely possible. More to say below responding to monteparnas.<br /> <br /> I don't know if being able to absorb Tass into your Pattern with Prime &gt;3 is a big deal to me, but the idea of not being able to use it *at all* without Prime 3 seems to really disrupt the idea of it being used commonly for trade among Mages. It would make it completely unusable for a lot of them, which would seem to make it into more of a niche commodity for Wonder-makers and other Prime specialists. And those people would end up with a very central role in the Awakened community, acting as something like moneychangers for local Mages stuck with Tass they can't use, especially since M20 seems to say that all Nodes produce some of their Quint as Tass.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538253#post1538253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to Tass, how you use it is important.<br /> <br /> My understanding (I don't remember if and where I read it) is that Tass can be directly used in spellcasting, as long as it is done in an appropriate way. And that would make its Resonance very important to consider.<br /> <br /> So, let's say you have a vial of Vampire Blood counting as Tass, and you want to make mind-altering spell. One way to do so could be to inscribe runes in the tied up target's head with red ink, and then you incorporate the Vitae by using it as said ink. The resonance of the Vitae would be relevant in the casting, though, helping or hindering depending on what kinds of thoughts you want to create.<br /> <br /> This would be a Prime-Free use of Tass. Vampire Blood is a special case in that a Mage that consumes it will keep it as Vitae, which is Quintessence in itself, but most other Tass can't be consumed for later use without Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does make more sense than just being able to use it without any special consideration (aside from Resonance, of course) without any skill with Prime. I was already thinking something along those lines after posting, and it seemed like the sort of thing that would be especially useful for ritual casting, where you have time to carefully consider how to incorporate the Tass. And it would make it important to find Tass that is compatible with your Practice and Instruments.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the more I thought about Blood Treachery, the more I kind of remember the perk being that it was &quot;extra&quot; Quint on top of what could be stored in the Pattern normally, and probably not accessible to being drained with just Prime 3, kind of like the personal Quint held by the Avatar. And yeah, given that Vitae has supernatural effects on even Sleepers that drink it, it would make sense that the Quint inside would be uniquely accessible. Still a bloody stupid idea, pun intended.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback so far, everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T13:12:20-07:00","id":1538315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538247#post1538247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think the rule for Nodes is that a mage can meditate in the presence of one to absorb Quint even without Prime, but the limit is the Avatar rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely this. Any Mage can meditate in a Node in order to replenish his Quint pool up to his Avatar rate. This doesn't require any level of Prime at all. The Mage's Avatar serves as a &quot;sponge&quot;, absorbing the free flowing Quint into it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With Prime 1 there isn't a limit anymore. </div> </div> </div>Precisely. You need Prime 1 in order to hold more Quint than what your Avatar allows. It's like &quot;forcing&quot; the Quint to stay inside of you beyond your limit. This can be done in order to absorb Quint in any free form, be it from free floating Quint from a Node or immediately after liberating Quint from a Tass, or even after using a &quot;dematerialization attack&quot; in a Pattern with Prime 4, that... Well, it is the best description to it, you literally &quot;dematerialize&quot; a Pattern, returning it to pure Quintessence.<br /> <br /> In the case of Tass or a &quot;dematerialized&quot; Pattern, you must immediately &quot;suck up&quot; the Quint that is liberated, otherwise it gets dissipated into the &quot;cosmic background radiation&quot; (imagine for a minute that the real world &quot;cosmic background radiation&quot;, which exists everywhere, is like the Quintessence, that also exists everywhere. When you &quot;liberate&quot; the Quint, it is in a extremely &quot;concentrated&quot; form, which can be captured and used. However, if not used, it just dissipates into the overall &quot;cosmic background radiation&quot; that is too &quot;dispersed&quot; to be usable, unless you use Prime 4 to &quot;suck up&quot; from that same &quot;cosmic background radiation&quot;. Prime 4, in this instance, would function as a &quot;condensator&quot; of that &quot;cosmic background radiation&quot;, concentrating it in a form once again usable)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Converting Tass, though, still takes Prime 3. While the description of Prime 1 does indicate otherwise, the first rank of Spheres generally doesn't augment a mage's capabilities like that. General Tass conversion should remain Rank 3 </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, using Prime 1 to absorb Tass by eating it (or in some other appropriate way consuming it) makes a lot of sense thematically. I think it might even be a rule in previous editions or in Awakening. If you want to rule that Prime 1 allows a mage to absorb the Quintessence of Tass when it is used/consumed in a dramatically appropriate mundane way, that would be quite reasonable. </div> </div> </div>That indeed makes a lot of sense. Biological patterns work by transmuting the Quintessence inside of Patterns; that is explicitly said in both 2nd and 3rd editions (I don't remember if it is also explained in M20, but it probably is). So, although it isn't said anywhere, I would absolutely approve to allow edible Tass to be absorbed using merely Prime 1, since the body will indeed be absorbing the relevant Quint stored in the Tass into it.<br /> <br /> Besides, that's one hell of a cool concept, allowing for weird and cool stuff to happen, like eating bones Tass in order to allow for some extra Quint for Mages not so well versed in Prime. And the &quot;Rule of Cool&quot; approves that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T13:23:37-07:00","id":1538317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538258#post1538258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand the rules for meditating at Nodes and their relationship to Prime, they're pretty clear.<br /> <br /> There are a bunch of other weird things that you can do with Prime 1 that wouldn't normally be possible with the sensory nature of the first rank in a Sphere (I think I saw Ambrosia harrumphing about it in one thread I was reading? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). I've also wondered the same thing about getting Mind Shields with Mind 1. So I considered it an open question. But yeah, M20 can be a bit of a mess sometimes even in the basic description of the Spheres (e.g. arguments about that paragraph saying you need Matter or Life for teleporting small objects with Correspondence 2).<br /> <br /> I do think that my memories about being able to consume certain forms of Tass may be coming from my time with Awakening, entirely possible. More to say below responding to monteparnas.<br /> <br /> I don't know if being able to absorb Tass into your Pattern with Prime &gt;3 is a big deal to me, but the idea of not being able to use it *at all* without Prime 3 seems to really disrupt the idea of it being used commonly for trade among Mages. It would make it completely unusable for a lot of them, which would seem to make it into more of a niche commodity for Wonder-makers and other Prime specialists. And those people would end up with a very central role in the Awakened community, acting as something like moneychangers for local Mages stuck with Tass they can't use, especially since M20 seems to say that all Nodes produce some of their Quint as Tass.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That does make more sense than just being able to use it without any special consideration (aside from Resonance, of course) without any skill with Prime. I was already thinking something along those lines after posting, and it seemed like the sort of thing that would be especially useful for ritual casting, where you have time to carefully consider how to incorporate the Tass. And it would make it important to find Tass that is compatible with your Practice and Instruments.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the more I thought about Blood Treachery, the more I kind of remember the perk being that it was &quot;extra&quot; Quint on top of what could be stored in the Pattern normally, and probably not accessible to being drained with just Prime 3, kind of like the personal Quint held by the Avatar. And yeah, given that Vitae has supernatural effects on even Sleepers that drink it, it would make sense that the Quint inside would be uniquely accessible. Still a bloody stupid idea, pun intended.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback so far, everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's an awesome idea! 100% agreed upon everything! The rule of cool approves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T15:28:43-07:00","id":1538396,"title":"","content":"As long as the Tass is in the form of one of your instruments and you can incorporate it in to your practice. You can just use the quintessence it contains. So if you have a node that produces quintessence apples, you can turn them in to cyder and use said cyder as an offering to the gods. If you have a cave node which make chalky deposits as tass, you can gather up that chalk and grind it to a fine powder which you can then sprinkle over your ritual circle to incorporate that tass in to your effect.<br /> <br /> You do not need to have quintessence in your wheel in order to use it, you can just use the quintessence from the tass. That is one of the reasons tass is used as currency in mage society, it's a way for mages to make use of quintessence even if they have Avatar 0 and now sense of Prime<br /> Speak<br /> <br /> The important thing is that you have to destroy the tass to release the quintessence from it in to your effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-10-2024, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T19:07:03-07:00","id":1538401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538396#post1538396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as the Tass is in the form of one of your instruments and you can incorporate it in to your practice. You can just use the quintessence it contains. So if you have a node that produces quintessence apples, you can turn them in to cyder and use said cyder as an offering to the gods. If you have a cave node which make chalky deposits as tass, you can gather up that chalk and grind it to a fine powder which you can then sprinkle over your ritual circle to incorporate that tass in to your effect.<br /> <br /> You do not need to have quintessence in your wheel in order to use it, you can just use the quintessence from the tass. That is one of the reasons tass is used as currency in mage society, it's a way for mages to make use of quintessence even if they have Avatar 0 and now sense of Prime<br /> Speak<br /> <br /> The important thing is that you have to destroy the tass to release the quintessence from it in to your effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is that the text is very confusing on the matter. I agree that this is possibly the best way to look at it, but the descriptions on Prime's levels also claim at the same time that you do require Prime 3 to use Tass (which, I agree, is pretty out of place)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T19:17:28-07:00","id":1538404,"title":"","content":"The section on Quintessence says Prime 3 for Tass as well. However, I think we have to distinguish between two different things: using Tass in dramatically appropriate ways vs converting it straight into personal Quintessence. Prime 3 is clearly the rank for the latter but it doesn\u2019t make sense for the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T19:21:00-07:00","id":1538405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538404#post1538404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The section on Quintessence says Prime 3 for Tass as well. However, I think we have to distinguish between two different things: using Tass in dramatically appropriate ways vs converting it straight into personal Quintessence. Prime 3 is clearly the rank for the latter but it doesn\u2019t make sense for the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But that's the problem, the text is very confusing (as usual). I do agree that using Tass in an appropriate way should be &quot;free&quot; (provided that you use the item in some way), but it's hard to infer that from the holy books","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T14:03:46-07:00","id":1538446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538401#post1538401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem is that the text is very confusing on the matter. I agree that this is possibly the best way to look at it, but the descriptions on Prime's levels also claim at the same time that you do require Prime 3 to use Tass (which, I agree, is pretty out of place)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, it says you require Prime 3 to move the quintessence from the tass to your own wheel. But if you destroy the tass, the quintessence simply releases, since there is nothing to hold it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T14:34:57-07:00","id":1538449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538446#post1538446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you destroy the tass, the quintessence simply releases, since there is nothing to hold it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Releasing the Quintessence by destroying the Tass isn't necessarily the same thing as being able to harness that Quint for a Mage's spell, however. Do you have an explicit source supporting Tass being used that way? Hoping for some RAW confirmation if possible.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 explicitly let you use Tass for Charms in the Revised corebook, so that's something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T20:32:08-07:00","id":1538457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538446#post1538446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite, it says you require Prime 3 to move the quintessence from the tass to your own wheel. But if you destroy the tass, the quintessence simply releases, since there is nothing to hold it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538449#post1538449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Releasing the Quintessence by destroying the Tass isn't necessarily the same thing as being able to harness that Quint for a Mage's spell, however. Do you have an explicit source supporting Tass being used that way? Hoping for some RAW confirmation if possible.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 explicitly let you use Tass for Charms in the Revised corebook, so that's something.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that's what I was referring to. It may even be that this was supposed to be the writers original intent, but they never made it clear. It's not explicitly claimed that releasing the Quint from the Tass allows you to use for effects without the usage of Prime. All that is written about it is that you need Prime 3 in order to absorb it.<br /> <br /> I agree that it does make sense and that it should be like that that you can use Quint from Tass into effects without needing Prime, but I can't remember anywhere where it is stated to be so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T20:23:14-07:00","id":1538550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538449#post1538449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hoping for some RAW confirmation if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll get none. It is just an interesting and useful interpretation that incorporating Tass in your magic lets you apply the Quint without Prime.<br /> <br /> By how the books describe Tass as Awakened Currency, it may even be considered possible RAI. But RAW is just silent in the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T17:49:17-07:00","id":1538592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538550#post1538550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll get none. It is just an interesting and useful interpretation that incorporating Tass in your magic lets you apply the Quint without Prime.<br /> <br /> By how the books describe Tass as Awakened Currency, it may even be considered possible RAI. But RAW is just silent in the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>*shakes fist at the heavens*</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback, everybody. Unless somebody has another source to quote on the matter, it seems like I've got the general opinion on the matter, the rest is up to Storyteller discretion. In my case, I think I'll stick with the consensus here that you can use Tass to help power a spell if you find a way to incorporate it into the Instruments or ritual methods appropriate for your Practice.<br /> <br /> I'm on the fence about house-ruling that a Mage with Prime 2 can directly pull Quint out of Tass for a spell, but not being able to absorb it into your Pattern until Prime 3 per RAW.<br /> <br /> I've got another Quintessence-related question I may be bringing here soon, rather than starting another thread, but I want to double-check and make sure I can't work it out on my own first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T23:24:56-07:00","id":1538598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538237-quintessence-and-tass-usage?p=1538592#post1538592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>*shakes fist at the heavens*</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback, everybody. Unless somebody has another source to quote on the matter, it seems like I've got the general opinion on the matter, the rest is up to Storyteller discretion. In my case, I think I'll stick with the consensus here that you can use Tass to help power a spell if you find a way to incorporate it into the Instruments or ritual methods appropriate for your Practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a fellow ST who likewise is an upholder of the Golden Rule, I absolutely say that this is how you should do it.<br /> <br /> And the rule of cool agrees with me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm on the fence about house-ruling that a Mage with Prime 2 can directly pull Quint out of Tass for a spell, but not being able to absorb it into your Pattern until Prime 3 per RAW. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wouldn't do that one however. Unless the Tass is swallowed by the Mage (and is something that is actually digestable). But in that case, I would go for Prime 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've got another Quintessence-related question I may be bringing here soon, rather than starting another thread, but I want to double-check and make sure I can't work it out on my own first. </div> </div> </div>Oh comon, now you've made me curious about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}